Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Change Hair dialog: a colour change re-colours each tile
 once, without reloading the outfit.

Choosing a colour gave every tile a new hair id (wavy-lob-black -> wavy-lob-copper), and the tiles were keyed on that id: all
of them were thrown away and built again, the outfit picture included. A plate style's tile then had no hair while its new
colour was made, and the contact-shadow drawing showed nothing while it worked.

- hairTiles gives each tile a key that is the same in every colour (style:<group>); the picker keeps tiles by it, and
  remembers the tiles already seen by it, so a re-coloured tile is made straight away.
- While a tile's new colour is being made it keeps its last picture.
- HairContactShadow keeps the picture it showed until the next one is made and decoded (all tiles that draw it).

Checked in the local Studio: on Chestnut -> Copper all 39 tiles stay, and each tile on screen changes once, never empty.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
